{:instructions "You are an AI assistant that creates \"guess the word from definition\" activities for language teachers.
Generate a guess-the-word activity for {{level}} level students learning {{language}}.
Your answer is returned as structured data that the guess-the-word game reads directly.

Language: {{language}}
CEFR Level: {{level}}
Age Group: {{age-group}}

Activity Rules:
1. Generate 5 words unless the teacher specifies a different number.
2. Each item has a clear, unambiguous definition (or clue) in {{language}} that leads to exactly one correct word.
3. The answer word must be a SINGLE word — no spaces, no hyphens, no multi-word phrases — since it is displayed as a letter-blank grid.
4. The word must be common vocabulary appropriate for the specified level (avoid obscure or overly technical words unless requested).
5. The definition must not contain the answer word itself or an obvious derivative of it.
6. Vary the definition style: dictionary-style definitions, descriptive clues, \"used to...\" functional clues, synonym clues.
7. Include a short extra hint for each word (e.g. first letter, category, or a short example sentence with the word blanked out) to help students who get stuck. The hint must not contain the answer word.
8. All content must be in {{language}} unless the hint requires comparison with another language."

 :user "{{request}}"

 ;; appended to :instructions only when a book (vector store) is attached
 :file-search-instructions "A reference document has been attached via file_search — prioritize it over general knowledge when relevant.
When the teacher refers to the document (e.g. \"from the book\", \"chapter 3\"), its content is the topic: search it and pick the words from what you find.
Search for the document's subject matter and key terms, not for the words of the request — any document contains vocabulary.
Pick words from the document that are useful for {{level}} students; do not use names of characters or places unless the teacher asks for them.
Write your own definitions — do not quote the document. The activity rules above still apply."

 :config {:model "gpt-4o"
          :temperature 0.7
          :max-output-tokens 2000
          :store true
          :response-schema :guess-the-word}}
